content:
Linking through **`lorik.me`** gives you a clean personal root domain with dedicated subdomains or subpaths for your entire ecosystem.

Here is a recommended domain routing structure:

---

### 🌐 Recommended Domain & Routing Topology

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph lorik_me ["lorik.me (Personal Root & Portfolio Hub)"]
        Root["lorik.me / www.lorik.me — Main Sovereign Portal & Portfolio"]
    end

    subgraph Subdomains ["Subdomains & Reverse Proxy on RackNerd VPS"]
        D1["signal.lorik.me  --> SignalStack Discovery Engine"]
        D2["hub.lorik.me     --> artkitty.net Ecosystem Index & Sandbox"]
        D3["books.lorik.me   --> Calibre OPDS / LC-MD WebDAV Reader"]
        D4["box.lorik.me     --> MyBlackBox Microlog Dashboard"]
        D5["alist.lorik.me   --> Alist Multi-Cloud Storage Bridge"]
    end

    Root --> D1
    Root --> D2
    Root --> D3
    Root --> D4
    Root --> D5
```

---

### 🚀 Nginx Configuration for `lorik.me` (VPS)

On the RackNerd node, you can route all services through Nginx with minimal memory footprint (~10MB RAM):

```nginx
# 1. Main Portal & Central Ecosystem Index
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name lorik.me www.lorik.me hub.lorik.me artkitty.net;

    root /var/www/artkitty_portal;
    index index.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }
}

# 2. Calibre OPDS & Reader Service
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name books.lorik.me;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8083; # Calibre / OPDS port
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    }
}

# 3. Alist Multi-Cloud Storage Bridge
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name alist.lorik.me;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5244; # Default Alist port
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    }
}
```

---

### 📋 DNS Records Setup (e.g. Cloudflare / Namecheap)

Point the following **A Records** to your VPS IP (`104.223.122.158`):

| Type | Name / Host | Value / Target | TTL |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A** | `@` (`lorik.me`) | `104.223.122.158` | Auto |
| **A** | `hub` (`hub.lorik.me`) | `104.223.122.158` | Auto |
| **A** | `books` (`books.lorik.me`) | `104.223.122.158` | Auto |
| **A** | `alist` (`alist.lorik.me`) | `104.223.122.158` | Auto |
| **CNAME** | `artkitty.net` | `lorik.me` | Auto |

---

### Advantages of using `lorik.me`:
1. **Unified Identity**: Centralizes `artkitty.net`, `Meow`, `LC-MD`, and `MyBlackBox` under your primary brand while preserving `artkitty.net` as an alias/CNAME.
2. **Simplified SSL**: One wildcard Let's Encrypt certificate (`*.lorik.me`) covers all microservices with zero per-domain configuration overhead.
3. **Flexible Subdomains**: Easy to spin up sandbox environments like `test.lorik.me` or `demo.lorik.me` without modifying root records.

